WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Two classes sit the same
test, marked out of 12.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.770
Class A: 6, 6, 6, 6, 6, 6.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:14.180
Class B: 2, 10, 3, 9, 2, 10.

4
00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:18.740
The teacher adds up each class's marks
and divides by how many there are.

5
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:20.780
Both means: 6.

6
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.620
"Same average," she says.

7
00:00:22.670 --> 00:00:24.710
"So the classes are the same."

8
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.860
Is she right?

9
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.180
What could an average be hiding?

10
00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.460
In this mission, you'll work out the mean,

11
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:33.580
median and mode, three kinds of average.

12
00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.280
And you'll meet the range:
highest minus lowest.

13
00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:41.640
Your mission: find out what two
matching averages could be hiding.
